    The default S3 simplification pool cannot see through the constant offset
    (V + K) plus the sub-register sign test, so the convoluted boolean leaks into
    the rendered C instead of collapsing to a clean signed less-than.

    Stage / sub-stage: S3 simplification-quiescence (new named rule RuleOvLessSimplify).
    The rule is always on: assertion #2 proves it collapses the condition to
    a clean `cVar5 < '\b'` (signed byte compare against 8), and #1 that the
    OV-flag garbage condition never appears.
-->
